IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb1-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part V, sections 24 to 29.1: shares, their
-- issue, the consideration for them, the stated capital account, shares in series, the pre-emptive right,
-- and options and rights (including the bearer-form restriction). A corporation's holding of its own
-- shares and the solvency tests are in cb1-part5-own-shares.l4; reductions of capital, dividends and
-- the other sections up to 45 are in cb1-part5-capital-dividends.l4.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Each rule is named `<what it decides> within s <section>`. Money is a NUMBER of dollars
-- and a name that holds one ends "in dollars". A rule about the stated capital account assumes that the
-- stated capital provisions apply to the corporation; section 26(11) takes an open-end mutual fund out of
-- them, and its own rule is below.

§ `Part V -- Corporate finance, shares and stated capital (s 24 to s 29.1)`

§§ `s 24 shares`

-- s 24(1) and s 24(2): "registered form" and "without nominal or par value"; a share with nominal or par
-- value issued by a body corporate before it was continued under this Act is, for s 24(1), deemed to be
-- without it.
-- src:435 | 24 (1) Shares of a corporation shall be in registered form and shall be without nominal or par value.
-- src:437 | (2) When a body corporate is continued under this Act, a share with nominal or par value issued by the body corporate before it was so continued is, for the purpose of subsection (1), deemed to be a share without nominal or par value.
@ref CBCA s 24(1), s 24(2) shares (src:435 src:437)
GIVEN `the share is in registered form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share has a nominal or par value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share was issued by a body corporate before it was continued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the share is as s 24(1) requires within s 24(1) and s 24(2)` MEANS
        `the share is in registered form`
    AND (    (NOT `the share has a nominal or par value`)
          OR `the share was issued by a body corporate before it was continued under this Act`)

-- s 24(3): where a corporation has only one class of shares, the holders' rights are equal in all respects
-- and include the right to vote, to receive any dividend declared, and to receive the remaining property
-- on dissolution.
-- src:439 | (3) Where a corporation has only one class of shares, the rights of the holders thereof are equal in all respects and include the rights
-- src:440 | (a) to vote at any meeting of shareholders of the corporation;
-- src:441 | (b) to receive any dividend declared by the corporation; and
-- src:442 | (c) to receive the remaining property of the corporation on dissolution.
@ref CBCA s 24(3) rights attached to shares (src:439-442)
DECLARE `Right of a holder of shares (s 24(3))` IS ONE OF
    `to vote at any meeting of shareholders of the corporation`
    `to receive any dividend declared by the corporation`
    `to receive the remaining property of the corporation on dissolution`
    `any other right`

-- src:439 | (3) Where a corporation has only one class of shares, the rights of the holders thereof are equal in all respects and include the rights
-- src:440 | (a) to vote at any meeting of shareholders of the corporation;
-- src:441 | (b) to receive any dividend declared by the corporation; and
-- src:442 | (c) to receive the remaining property of the corporation on dissolution.
@ref CBCA s 24(3) rights attached to shares (src:439-442)
GIVEN `the corporation has only one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      right IS A `Right of a holder of shares (s 24(3))`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the holders of the only class have the right within s 24(3)` MEANS
    IF `the corporation has only one class of shares`
    THEN CONSIDER right
         WHEN `to vote at any meeting of shareholders of the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `to receive any dividend declared by the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `to receive the remaining property of the corporation on dissolution` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `any other right` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:439 | (3) Where a corporation has only one class of shares, the rights of the holders thereof are equal in all respects and include the rights
@ref CBCA s 24(3) rights attached to shares (src:439)
GIVEN `the corporation has only one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights of the holders are equal in all respects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the rights of the holders of the only class are as s 24(3) requires` MEANS
    `the corporation has only one class of shares` IMPLIES `the rights of the holders are equal in all respects`

-- s 24(4): "The articles may provide for more than one class of shares and, if they so provide," (a) the
-- rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to each class shall be set out in them; and
-- (b) the rights in subsection (3) shall be attached to at least one class, "but all such rights are not
-- required to be attached to one class": each may be on a different class.
-- src:444 | (4) The articles may provide for more than one class of shares and, if they so provide,
-- src:445 | (a) the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to the shares of each class shall be set out therein; and
-- src:446 | (b) the rights set out in subsection (3) shall be attached to at least one class of shares but all such rights are not required to be attached to one class.
@ref CBCA s 24(4) rights to classes of shares (src:444-446)
GIVEN `the articles provide for more than one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to the shares of each class are set out in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right to vote at any meeting of shareholders is attached to at least one class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right to receive any dividend declared is attached to at least one class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right to receive the remaining property of the corporation on dissolution is attached to at least one class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles meet the requirements for classes of shares within s 24(4)` MEANS
    `the articles provide for more than one class of shares`
    IMPLIES (    `the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to the shares of each class are set out in the articles`
             AND `the right to vote at any meeting of shareholders is attached to at least one class`
             AND `the right to receive any dividend declared is attached to at least one class`
             AND `the right to receive the remaining property of the corporation on dissolution is attached to at least one class`)

§§ `s 25 issue of shares`

-- s 25(1): "Subject to the articles, the by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement and to section 28",
-- shares may be issued at such times, to such persons and for such consideration as the directors
-- determine. The rule says whether the directors may determine; what they determine is theirs.
-- src:448 | 25 (1) Subject to the articles, the by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement and to section 28, shares may be issued at such times and to such persons and for such consideration as the directors may determine.
@ref CBCA s 25(1) issue of shares (src:448)
GIVEN `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement restrict the determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 28 restricts the determination because shareholders have a pre-emptive right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may determine the times, persons and consideration of an issue of shares within s 25(1)` MEANS
        (NOT `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement restrict the determination`)
    AND (NOT `section 28 restricts the determination because shareholders have a pre-emptive right`)

-- s 25(2): shares issued are non-assessable and the holders are not liable to the corporation or its
-- creditors "in respect thereof". JUST FALSE for an issued share; NOTHING for anything else, which the
-- subsection does not address.
-- src:450 | (2) Shares issued by a corporation are non-assessable and the holders are not liable to the corporation or to its creditors in respect thereof.
@ref CBCA s 25(2) shares non-assessable (src:450)
GIVEN `the share has been issued by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the holder is liable in respect of the share to the corporation or its creditors within s 25(2)` MEANS
    IF `the share has been issued by the corporation`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:452 | (3) A share shall not be issued until the consideration for the share is fully paid in money or in property or past services that are not less in value than the fair equivalent of the money that the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money.
@ref CBCA s 25(3) consideration (src:452)
DECLARE `Kind of consideration for a share (s 25(3))` IS ONE OF
    `money`
    `property`
    `past services`
    `any other consideration`

-- s 25(5): "property does not include a promissory note, or a promise to pay, that is made by a person to
-- whom a share is issued, or a person who does not deal at arm's length, within the meaning of that
-- expression in the Income Tax Act, with a person to whom a share is issued".
-- src:456 | (5) For the purposes of this section, property does not include a promissory note, or a promise to pay, that is made by a person to whom a share is issued, or a person who does not deal at arm’s length, within the meaning of that expression in the Income Tax Act, with a person to whom a share is issued.
@ref CBCA s 25(5) definition of property (src:456)
GIVEN `the thing is property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a promissory note or a promise to pay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made by a person to whom a share is issued, or by a person who does not deal at arm's length with a person to whom a share is issued` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: "arm's length" in the Income Tax Act (outside the Act)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the thing is property for the purposes of s 25 within s 25(5)` MEANS
        `the thing is property`
    AND (NOT (    `the thing is a promissory note or a promise to pay`
              AND `it is made by a person to whom a share is issued, or by a person who does not deal at arm's length with a person to whom a share is issued`))

-- s 25(3): "A share shall not be issued until the consideration for the share is fully paid in money or in
-- property or past services that are not less in value than the fair equivalent of the money that the
-- corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money."
-- src:452 | (3) A share shall not be issued until the consideration for the share is fully paid in money or in property or past services that are not less in value than the fair equivalent of the money that the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money.
@ref CBCA s 25(3) consideration (src:452)
GIVEN consideration IS A `Kind of consideration for a share (s 25(3))`
      `the consideration is fully paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value is not less than the fair equivalent of the money that the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is property for the purposes of s 25 under subsection 25(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the share may be issued for the consideration within s 25(3)` MEANS
        `the consideration is fully paid`
    AND CONSIDER consideration
        WHEN `money` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `property` THEN `the property is property for the purposes of s 25 under subsection 25(5)` AND `the value is not less than the fair equivalent of the money that the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money`
        WHEN `past services` THEN `the value is not less than the fair equivalent of the money that the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money`
        WHEN `any other consideration` THEN FALSE

-- s 25(4): in determining the fair equivalent, the directors "may take into account" two kinds of item.
-- The subsection permits these two and says nothing of others, so any other item is NOTHING.
-- src:454 | (4) In determining whether property or past services are the fair equivalent of a money consideration, the directors may take into account reasonable charges and expenses of organization and reorganization and payments for property and past services reasonably expected to benefit the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 25(4) consideration other than money (src:454)
DECLARE `Item the directors may take into account (s 25(4))` IS ONE OF
    `reasonable charges and expenses of organization and reorganization`
    `payments for property and past services reasonably expected to benefit the corporation`
    `any other item`

-- src:454 | (4) In determining whether property or past services are the fair equivalent of a money consideration, the directors may take into account reasonable charges and expenses of organization and reorganization and payments for property and past services reasonably expected to benefit the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 25(4) consideration other than money (src:454)
GIVEN item IS AN `Item the directors may take into account (s 25(4))`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the directors may take the item into account in determining the fair equivalent within s 25(4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reasonable charges and expenses of organization and reorganization` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `payments for property and past services reasonably expected to benefit the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any other item` THEN NOTHING

§§ `s 26 stated capital account`

-- src:458 | 26 (1) A corporation shall maintain a separate stated capital account for each class and series of shares it issues.
@ref CBCA s 26(1) stated capital account (src:458)
GIVEN `a separate stated capital account is maintained for each class and series of shares the corporation issues` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has complied with the duty to maintain stated capital accounts within s 26(1)` MEANS
    `a separate stated capital account is maintained for each class and series of shares the corporation issues`

-- s 26(3): the exchanges in which a corporation may add less than the full consideration.
-- src:462 | (3) Despite subsection (2), a corporation may, subject to subsection (4), add to the stated capital accounts maintained for the shares of classes or series the whole or any part of the amount of the consideration that it receives in an exchange if the corporation issues shares
-- src:463 | (a) in exchange for
-- src:464 | (i) property of a person who immediately before the exchange did not deal with the corporation at arm’s length within the meaning of that expression in the Income Tax Act,
-- src:465 | (ii) shares of, or another interest or right in, a body corporate that immediately before the exchange, or that because of the exchange, did not deal with the corporation at arm’s length within the meaning of that expression in the Income Tax Act, or
-- src:466 | (iii) property of a person who, immediately before the exchange, dealt with the corporation at arm’s length within the meaning of that expression in the Income Tax Act, if the person, the corporation and all the holders of shares in the class or series of shares so issued consent to the exchange; or
-- src:467 | (b) pursuant to an agreement referred to in subsection 182(1) or an arrangement referred to in paragraph 192(1)(b) or (c) or to shareholders of an amalgamating body corporate who receive the shares in addition to or instead of securities of the amalgamated body corporate.
@ref CBCA s 26(3) exception for non-arm's length transactions (src:462-467)
DECLARE `Exchange in which shares are issued (s 26(3))` IS ONE OF
    `in exchange for property of a person who immediately before the exchange did not deal with the corporation at arm's length`
    `in exchange for shares of, or another interest or right in, a body corporate that immediately before the exchange, or because of the exchange, did not deal with the corporation at arm's length`
    `in exchange for property of a person who dealt with the corporation at arm's length, and the person, the corporation and all the holders of shares in the class or series so issued consent to the exchange`
    `pursuant to an agreement referred to in subsection 182(1) or an arrangement referred to in paragraph 192(1)(b) or (c), or to shareholders of an amalgamating body corporate who receive the shares in addition to or instead of securities of the amalgamated body corporate`
    `any other issue of shares`

-- src:462 | (3) Despite subsection (2), a corporation may, subject to subsection (4), add to the stated capital accounts maintained for the shares of classes or series the whole or any part of the amount of the consideration that it receives in an exchange if the corporation issues shares
-- src:463 | (a) in exchange for
-- src:464 | (i) property of a person who immediately before the exchange did not deal with the corporation at arm’s length within the meaning of that expression in the Income Tax Act,
-- src:465 | (ii) shares of, or another interest or right in, a body corporate that immediately before the exchange, or that because of the exchange, did not deal with the corporation at arm’s length within the meaning of that expression in the Income Tax Act, or
-- src:466 | (iii) property of a person who, immediately before the exchange, dealt with the corporation at arm’s length within the meaning of that expression in the Income Tax Act, if the person, the corporation and all the holders of shares in the class or series of shares so issued consent to the exchange; or
-- src:467 | (b) pursuant to an agreement referred to in subsection 182(1) or an arrangement referred to in paragraph 192(1)(b) or (c) or to shareholders of an amalgamating body corporate who receive the shares in addition to or instead of securities of the amalgamated body corporate.
@ref CBCA s 26(3) exception for non-arm's length transactions (src:462-467)
GIVEN exchange IS AN `Exchange in which shares are issued (s 26(3))`
      `the person, the corporation and all the holders of shares in the class or series so issued consent to the exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may add less than the full consideration within s 26(3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER exchange
    WHEN `in exchange for property of a person who immediately before the exchange did not deal with the corporation at arm's length` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in exchange for shares of, or another interest or right in, a body corporate that immediately before the exchange, or because of the exchange, did not deal with the corporation at arm's length` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in exchange for property of a person who dealt with the corporation at arm's length, and the person, the corporation and all the holders of shares in the class or series so issued consent to the exchange` THEN `the person, the corporation and all the holders of shares in the class or series so issued consent to the exchange`
    WHEN `pursuant to an agreement referred to in subsection 182(1) or an arrangement referred to in paragraph 192(1)(b) or (c), or to shareholders of an amalgamating body corporate who receive the shares in addition to or instead of securities of the amalgamated body corporate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other issue of shares` THEN FALSE

-- s 26(2) and s 26(4): add "the full amount of any consideration it receives", and never "an amount
-- greater than the amount of the consideration it received for the share". Section 26(3) lets the amount be
-- "the whole or any part" in the listed exchanges, so only there may the amount added be less.
-- src:460 | (2) A corporation shall add to the appropriate stated capital account the full amount of any consideration it receives for any shares it issues.
-- src:462 | (3) Despite subsection (2), a corporation may, subject to subsection (4), add to the stated capital accounts maintained for the shares of classes or series the whole or any part of the amount of the consideration that it receives in an exchange if the corporation issues shares
-- src:469 | (4) On the issue of a share a corporation shall not add to a stated capital account in respect of the share it issues an amount greater than the amount of the consideration it received for the share.
@ref CBCA s 26(2), s 26(3), s 26(4) entries in stated capital account (src:460 src:462 src:469)
GIVEN `the amount of the consideration the corporation received, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount added to the stated capital account, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the corporation may add less than the full consideration under subsection 26(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the amount added to the stated capital account is permitted within s 26(2), s 26(3) and s 26(4)` MEANS
        `the amount added to the stated capital account, in dollars` AT MOST `the amount of the consideration the corporation received, in dollars`
    AND (    `the amount added to the stated capital account, in dollars` EQUALS `the amount of the consideration the corporation received, in dollars`
          OR `the corporation may add less than the full consideration under subsection 26(3)`)

-- s 26(5): an addition of an amount not received as consideration for the issue of shares, where there are
-- outstanding shares of more than one class or series, "must be approved by special resolution unless all
-- the issued and outstanding shares are shares of not more than two classes of convertible shares referred
-- to in subsection 39(5)".
-- src:471 | (5) Where a corporation proposes to add any amount to a stated capital account it maintains in respect of a class or series of shares, if
-- src:472 | (a) the amount to be added was not received by the corporation as consideration for the issue of shares, and
-- src:473 | (b) the corporation has issued any outstanding shares of more than one class or series,
-- src:474 | the addition to the stated capital account must be approved by special resolution unless all the issued and outstanding shares are shares of not more than two classes of convertible shares referred to in subsection 39(5).
@ref CBCA s 26(5) constraint on addition to a stated capital account (src:471-474)
GIVEN `the amount to be added was received by the corporation as consideration for the issue of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has issued outstanding shares of more than one class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the issued and outstanding shares are shares of not more than two classes of convertible shares referred to in subsection 39(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the addition must be approved by special resolution within s 26(5)` MEANS
        (NOT `the amount to be added was received by the corporation as consideration for the issue of shares`)
    AND `the corporation has issued outstanding shares of more than one class or series`
    AND (NOT `all the issued and outstanding shares are shares of not more than two classes of convertible shares referred to in subsection 39(5)`)

-- src:471 | (5) Where a corporation proposes to add any amount to a stated capital account it maintains in respect of a class or series of shares, if
-- src:472 | (a) the amount to be added was not received by the corporation as consideration for the issue of shares, and
-- src:473 | (b) the corporation has issued any outstanding shares of more than one class or series,
-- src:474 | the addition to the stated capital account must be approved by special resolution unless all the issued and outstanding shares are shares of not more than two classes of convertible shares referred to in subsection 39(5).
@ref CBCA s 26(5) constraint on addition to a stated capital account (src:471-474)
GIVEN `the addition must be approved by special resolution under subsection 26(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      tally IS A `Vote tally`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the addition has the approval s 26(5) requires` MEANS
    `the addition must be approved by special resolution under subsection 26(5)`
    IMPLIES `special resolution within s 2(1)` tally

-- s 26(6): a continued body corporate "may add to a stated capital account any consideration received by it
-- for a share it issued", and a corporation at any time may, "subject to subsection (5)", add any amount it
-- credited to a retained earnings or other surplus account.
-- src:476 | (6) When a body corporate is continued under this Act, it may add to a stated capital account any consideration received by it for a share it issued and a corporation at any time may, subject to subsection (5), add to a stated capital account any amount it credited to a retained earnings or other surplus account.
@ref CBCA s 26(6) other additions to stated capital (src:476)
DECLARE `Amount a corporation proposes to add to a stated capital account (s 26(6))` IS ONE OF
    `consideration received by a continued body corporate for a share it issued`
    `an amount credited to a retained earnings or other surplus account`
    `any other amount`

-- src:476 | (6) When a body corporate is continued under this Act, it may add to a stated capital account any consideration received by it for a share it issued and a corporation at any time may, subject to subsection (5), add to a stated capital account any amount it credited to a retained earnings or other surplus account.
@ref CBCA s 26(6) other additions to stated capital (src:476)
GIVEN amount IS AN `Amount a corporation proposes to add to a stated capital account (s 26(6))`
      `the body corporate was continued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the addition has the approval s 26(5) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the corporation may add the amount to a stated capital account within s 26(6)` MEANS
    CONSIDER amount
    WHEN `consideration received by a continued body corporate for a share it issued` THEN JUST `the body corporate was continued under this Act`
    WHEN `an amount credited to a retained earnings or other surplus account` THEN JUST `the addition has the approval s 26(5) requires`
    WHEN `any other amount` THEN NOTHING

-- s 26(7): a continued body corporate: subsection (2) "does not apply to the consideration received by it
-- before it was so continued unless the share in respect of which the consideration is received is issued
-- after the corporation is so continued".
-- src:478 | (7) When a body corporate is continued under this Act, subsection (2) does not apply to the consideration received by it before it was so continued unless the share in respect of which the consideration is received is issued after the corporation is so continued.
@ref CBCA s 26(7) transitional (src:478)
GIVEN `the body corporate was continued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consideration was received before the body corporate was continued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share in respect of which the consideration is received was issued after the corporation was continued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subsection 26(2) applies to the consideration within s 26(7)` MEANS
        (NOT (`the body corporate was continued under this Act` AND `the consideration was received before the body corporate was continued`))
    OR  `the share in respect of which the consideration is received was issued after the corporation was continued`

-- src:480 | (8) When a body corporate is continued under this Act, any amount unpaid in respect of a share issued by the body corporate before it was so continued and paid after it was so continued shall be added to the stated capital account maintained for the shares of that class or series.
@ref CBCA s 26(8) idem (src:480)
GIVEN `the body corporate was continued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an amount was unpaid in respect of a share issued by the body corporate before it was continued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount was paid after the body corporate was continued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must add the amount to the stated capital account for the class or series within s 26(8)` MEANS
        `the body corporate was continued under this Act`
    AND `an amount was unpaid in respect of a share issued by the body corporate before it was continued`
    AND `the amount was paid after the body corporate was continued`

-- s 26(9): for s 34(2), sections 38 and 42, and paragraph 185(2)(a), a continued body corporate's stated
-- capital "is deemed to include" the amount that would have been included had it been incorporated under
-- this Act. "Include" is read as a floor: the stated capital is at least that amount, and is the larger of
-- the two when the accounts already show more (fork cb1-F6 in NOTES.md).
-- src:482 | (9) For the purposes of subsection 34(2), sections 38 and 42, and paragraph 185(2)(a), when a body corporate is continued under this Act its stated capital is deemed to include the amount that would have been included in stated capital if the body corporate had been incorporated under this Act.
@ref CBCA s 26(9) transitional (src:482)
GIVEN `the body corporate was continued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stated capital shown in the accounts of the body corporate, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that would have been included in stated capital if the body corporate had been incorporated under this Act, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the stated capital of the body corporate for the purposes of s 34(2), s 38, s 42 and paragraph 185(2)(a) within s 26(9)` MEANS
    IF `the body corporate was continued under this Act`
    THEN max `the stated capital shown in the accounts of the body corporate, in dollars` `the amount that would have been included in stated capital if the body corporate had been incorporated under this Act, in dollars`
    ELSE `the stated capital shown in the accounts of the body corporate, in dollars`

-- src:484 | (10) A corporation shall not reduce its stated capital or any stated capital account except in the manner provided in this Act.
@ref CBCA s 26(10) restriction (src:484)
GIVEN `the reduction is made in a manner provided in this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may reduce its stated capital or a stated capital account within s 26(10)` MEANS
    `the reduction is made in a manner provided in this Act`

-- s 26(12): "open-end mutual fund means a distributing corporation that carries on only the business of
-- investing the consideration it receives for the shares it issues, and all or substantially all of those
-- shares are redeemable on the demand of a shareholder." s 26(11): subsections (1) to (10), and any other
-- provisions of this Act relating to stated capital, do not apply to one.
-- src:488 | (12) For the purposes of this section, open-end mutual fund means a distributing corporation that carries on only the business of investing the consideration it receives for the shares it issues, and all or substantially all of those shares are redeemable on the demand of a shareholder.
@ref CBCA s 26(12) definition of open-end mutual fund (src:488)
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 2(1) (keel)
      `the corporation carries on only the business of investing the consideration it receives for the shares it issues` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all or substantially all of its shares are redeemable on the demand of a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is an open-end mutual fund within s 26(12)` MEANS
        `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
    AND `the corporation carries on only the business of investing the consideration it receives for the shares it issues`
    AND `all or substantially all of its shares are redeemable on the demand of a shareholder`

-- src:486 | (11) Subsections (1) to (10) and any other provisions of this Act relating to stated capital do not apply to an open-end mutual fund.
@ref CBCA s 26(11) exception for an open-end mutual fund (src:486)
GIVEN `the corporation is an open-end mutual fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the stated capital provisions of this Act apply to the corporation within s 26(11)` MEANS
    NOT `the corporation is an open-end mutual fund`

§§ `s 27 shares in series`

-- src:490 | 27 (1) The articles may authorize, subject to any limitations set out in them, the issue of any class of shares in one or more series and may do either or both of the following:
-- src:491 | (a) fix the number of shares in, and determine the designation, rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to the shares of, each series; or
-- src:492 | (b) authorize the directors to fix the number of shares in, and determine the designation, rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to the shares of, each series.
@ref CBCA s 27(1) shares in series (src:490-492)
DECLARE `Way of fixing the terms of a series (s 27(1))` IS ONE OF
    `the articles fix the number of shares in, and determine the designation, rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to the shares of, each series`
    `the articles authorize the directors to fix the number of shares in, and determine the designation, rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to the shares of, each series`
    `any other way`

-- src:490 | 27 (1) The articles may authorize, subject to any limitations set out in them, the issue of any class of shares in one or more series and may do either or both of the following:
-- src:491 | (a) fix the number of shares in, and determine the designation, rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to the shares of, each series; or
-- src:492 | (b) authorize the directors to fix the number of shares in, and determine the designation, rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to the shares of, each series.
@ref CBCA s 27(1) shares in series (src:490-492)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of fixing the terms of a series (s 27(1))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles may authorize the issue of a class of shares in series in that way within s 27(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `the articles fix the number of shares in, and determine the designation, rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to the shares of, each series` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the articles authorize the directors to fix the number of shares in, and determine the designation, rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to the shares of, each series` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other way` THEN FALSE

-- s 27(2): if cumulative dividends or amounts payable on return of capital are not paid in full, the shares
-- of all series of the same class "participate rateably". Each series takes the available sum in the
-- proportion its claim bears to the claims of all series, and never more than its claim. NOTHING where no
-- series has a claim: the proportion has no meaning.
-- src:494 | (2) If any cumulative dividends or amounts payable on return of capital in respect of a series of shares are not paid in full, the shares of all series of the same class participate rateably in respect of accumulated dividends and return of capital.
@ref CBCA s 27(2) series participation (src:494)
GIVEN `the sum available for the accumulated dividends or the return of capital, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount owing to this series, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount owing to all series of the same class, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount this series receives within s 27(2)` MEANS
    IF `the amount owing to all series of the same class, in dollars` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (min `the amount owing to this series, in dollars` (`the sum available for the accumulated dividends or the return of capital, in dollars` TIMES `the amount owing to this series, in dollars` DIVIDED BY `the amount owing to all series of the same class, in dollars`))

-- src:496 | (3) No rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached to a series of shares authorized under this section shall confer on a series a priority in respect of dividends or return of capital over any other series of shares of the same class that are then outstanding.
@ref CBCA s 27(3) restrictions on series (src:496)
GIVEN `the rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions confer on the series a priority in respect of dividends or return of capital over another series of the same class that is then outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the rights attached to the series are permitted within s 27(3)` MEANS
    NOT `the rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions confer on the series a priority in respect of dividends or return of capital over another series of the same class that is then outstanding`

-- src:498 | (4) If the directors exercise their authority under paragraph (1)(b), they shall, before the issue of shares of the series, send, in the form that the Director fixes, articles of amendment to the Director to designate a series of shares.
@ref CBCA s 27(4) amendment of articles (src:498)
GIVEN `the directors exercise their authority under paragraph 27(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the articles of amendment designating the series were sent to the Director` IS A DATE
      `the day shares of the series were issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors have complied with the duty to send articles of amendment before the issue within s 27(4)` MEANS
        `the directors exercise their authority under paragraph 27(1)(b)`
    IMPLIES (NOT (`the day shares of the series were issued` AT MOST `the day the articles of amendment designating the series were sent to the Director`))

-- src:500 | (5) On receipt of articles of amendment designating a series of shares, the Director shall issue a certificate of amendment in accordance with section 262.
@ref CBCA s 27(5) certificate of amendment (src:500)
GIVEN `the Director has received articles of amendment designating a series of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must issue a certificate of amendment within s 27(5)` MEANS
    `the Director has received articles of amendment designating a series of shares`

-- src:502 | (6) The articles of the corporation are amended accordingly on the date shown in the certificate of amendment.
@ref CBCA s 27(6) effect of certificate (src:502)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles are amended by the certificate of amendment by the day within s 27(6)` MEANS
    day AT LEAST `the date shown in the certificate of amendment`

§§ `s 28 pre-emptive right`

-- src:504 | 28 (1) If the articles so provide, no shares of a class shall be issued unless the shares have first been offered to the shareholders holding shares of that class, and those shareholders have a pre-emptive right to acquire the offered shares in proportion to their holdings of the shares of that class, at such price and on such terms as those shares are to be offered to others.
-- src:506 | (2) Notwithstanding that the articles provide the pre-emptive right referred to in subsection (1), shareholders have no pre-emptive right in respect of shares to be issued
-- src:507 | (a) for a consideration other than money;
-- src:508 | (b) as a share dividend; or
-- src:509 | (c) pursuant to the exercise of conversion privileges, options or rights previously granted by the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 28(1), s 28(2) pre-emptive right (src:504 src:506-509)
DECLARE `Issue of shares (s 28(2))` IS ONE OF
    `shares to be issued for a consideration other than money`
    `shares to be issued as a share dividend`
    `shares to be issued pursuant to the exercise of conversion privileges, options or rights previously granted by the corporation`
    `any other issue of shares`

-- src:504 | 28 (1) If the articles so provide, no shares of a class shall be issued unless the shares have first been offered to the shareholders holding shares of that class, and those shareholders have a pre-emptive right to acquire the offered shares in proportion to their holdings of the shares of that class, at such price and on such terms as those shares are to be offered to others.
-- src:506 | (2) Notwithstanding that the articles provide the pre-emptive right referred to in subsection (1), shareholders have no pre-emptive right in respect of shares to be issued
-- src:507 | (a) for a consideration other than money;
-- src:508 | (b) as a share dividend; or
-- src:509 | (c) pursuant to the exercise of conversion privileges, options or rights previously granted by the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 28(1), s 28(2) pre-emptive right (src:504 src:506-509)
GIVEN `the articles provide for the pre-emptive right` IS A BOOLEAN
      issue IS AN `Issue of shares (s 28(2))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`shareholders of the class have a pre-emptive right in respect of the shares within s 28(1) and s 28(2)` MEANS
        `the articles provide for the pre-emptive right`
    AND CONSIDER issue
        WHEN `shares to be issued for a consideration other than money` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `shares to be issued as a share dividend` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `shares to be issued pursuant to the exercise of conversion privileges, options or rights previously granted by the corporation` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `any other issue of shares` THEN TRUE

-- "a pre-emptive right to acquire the offered shares in proportion to their holdings of the shares of that
-- class". NOTHING if no shares of the class are held.
-- src:504 | 28 (1) If the articles so provide, no shares of a class shall be issued unless the shares have first been offered to the shareholders holding shares of that class, and those shareholders have a pre-emptive right to acquire the offered shares in proportion to their holdings of the shares of that class, at such price and on such terms as those shares are to be offered to others.
@ref CBCA s 28(1) pre-emptive right (src:504)
GIVEN `the number of shares offered` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares of the class that the shareholder holds` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares of the class that all shareholders hold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the number of the offered shares the shareholder has a pre-emptive right to acquire within s 28(1)` MEANS
    IF `the number of shares of the class that all shareholders hold` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the number of shares offered` TIMES `the number of shares of the class that the shareholder holds` DIVIDED BY `the number of shares of the class that all shareholders hold`)

-- src:504 | 28 (1) If the articles so provide, no shares of a class shall be issued unless the shares have first been offered to the shareholders holding shares of that class, and those shareholders have a pre-emptive right to acquire the offered shares in proportion to their holdings of the shares of that class, at such price and on such terms as those shares are to be offered to others.
@ref CBCA s 28(1) pre-emptive right (src:504)
GIVEN `the articles provide for the pre-emptive right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares have first been offered to the shareholders holding shares of that class, at the price and on the terms on which they are to be offered to others` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are within the exceptions of subsection 28(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shares of the class may be issued within s 28(1)` MEANS
    (    `the articles provide for the pre-emptive right`
     AND (NOT `the shares are within the exceptions of subsection 28(2)`))
    IMPLIES `the shares have first been offered to the shareholders holding shares of that class, at the price and on the terms on which they are to be offered to others`

§§ `s 29 and s 29.1 options and rights; bearer form`

-- src:511 | 29 (1) A corporation may issue certificates, warrants or other evidences of conversion privileges, options or rights to acquire securities of the corporation, and shall set out the conditions thereof
-- src:512 | (a) in the certificates, warrants or other evidences; or
-- src:513 | (b) in certificates evidencing the securities to which the conversion privileges, options or rights are attached.
@ref CBCA s 29(1) options and rights (src:511-513)
GIVEN `the conditions are set out in the certificates, warrants or other evidences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions are set out in certificates evidencing the securities to which the conversion privileges, options or rights are attached` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has set out the conditions as s 29(1) requires` MEANS
        `the conditions are set out in the certificates, warrants or other evidences`
    OR  `the conditions are set out in certificates evidencing the securities to which the conversion privileges, options or rights are attached`

-- s 29(2): conversion privileges, options and rights "may be made transferable or non-transferable, and
-- options and rights to acquire may be made separable or inseparable from any securities to which they are
-- attached". Whether a conversion privilege may be made separable is not said, so it is NOTHING.
-- src:515 | (2) Conversion privileges, options and rights to acquire securities of a corporation may be made transferable or non-transferable, and options and rights to acquire may be made separable or inseparable from any securities to which they are attached.
@ref CBCA s 29(2) transferable rights (src:515)
DECLARE `Instrument under s 29(2)` IS ONE OF
    `a conversion privilege`
    `an option`
    `a right to acquire securities of the corporation`

-- src:515 | (2) Conversion privileges, options and rights to acquire securities of a corporation may be made transferable or non-transferable, and options and rights to acquire may be made separable or inseparable from any securities to which they are attached.
@ref CBCA s 29(2) transferable rights (src:515)
GIVEN instrument IS AN `Instrument under s 29(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instrument may be made transferable or non-transferable within s 29(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `a conversion privilege` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an option` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a right to acquire securities of the corporation` THEN TRUE

-- src:515 | (2) Conversion privileges, options and rights to acquire securities of a corporation may be made transferable or non-transferable, and options and rights to acquire may be made separable or inseparable from any securities to which they are attached.
@ref CBCA s 29(2) transferable rights (src:515)
GIVEN instrument IS AN `Instrument under s 29(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the instrument may be made separable or inseparable from the securities to which it is attached within s 29(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `a conversion privilege` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an option` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a right to acquire securities of the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE

-- s 29(3): "if the articles limit the number of authorized shares, the corporation shall reserve and continue
-- to reserve sufficient authorized shares to meet the exercise" of the conversion privileges, options and
-- rights it has granted.
-- src:517 | (3) Where a corporation has granted privileges to convert any securities issued by the corporation into shares, or into shares of another class or series, or has issued or granted options or rights to acquire shares, if the articles limit the number of authorized shares, the corporation shall reserve and continue to reserve sufficient authorized shares to meet the exercise of such conversion privileges, options and rights.
@ref CBCA s 29(3) reserved shares (src:517)
GIVEN `the articles limit the number of authorized shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of authorized shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares issued` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares needed to meet the exercise of the conversion privileges, options and rights` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has reserved sufficient authorized shares within s 29(3)` MEANS
    `the articles limit the number of authorized shares`
    IMPLIES (`the number of authorized shares` MINUS `the number of shares issued` AT LEAST `the number of shares needed to meet the exercise of the conversion privileges, options and rights`)

-- src:519 | 29.1 (1) Despite section 29, a corporation shall not issue, in bearer form, a certificate, warrant or other evidence of a conversion privilege, option or right to acquire a share of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 29.1(1) restriction regarding bearer shares (src:519)
GIVEN `the document is a certificate, warrant or other evidence of a conversion privilege, option or right to acquire a share of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is in bearer form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is forbidden to issue the document within s 29.1(1)` MEANS
        `the document is a certificate, warrant or other evidence of a conversion privilege, option or right to acquire a share of the corporation`
    AND `the document is in bearer form`

-- s 29.1(2): "issued before the coming into force of this section"; the day is not in the text, so whether
-- the document was issued before it is a plain fact.
-- src:521 | (2) A corporation shall, on the request of a holder of a certificate, warrant or other evidence of a conversion privilege, option or right to acquire a share of the corporation that is in bearer form and that was issued before the coming into force of this section, issue in exchange to that holder, in registered form, a certificate, warrant or other evidence, as the case may be.
@ref CBCA s 29.1(2) replacement (src:521)
GIVEN `the holder has requested an exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a certificate, warrant or other evidence of a conversion privilege, option or right to acquire a share of the corporation, in bearer form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document was issued before the coming into force of section 29.1` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the day section 29.1 came into force (not in the text)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must issue a registered document in exchange within s 29.1(2)` MEANS
        `the holder has requested an exchange`
    AND `the document is a certificate, warrant or other evidence of a conversion privilege, option or right to acquire a share of the corporation, in bearer form`
    AND `the document was issued before the coming into force of section 29.1`
